Input: {"question": "What is the profession of Andrew McFarlane?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d00", "start": 0, "end": 95, "text": "Andrew McFarlane (judge) Sir Andrew Ewart McFarlane, PC (born 20 June 1954) is a British judge."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d00", "start": 96, "end": 276, "text": "He was a Lord Justice of Appeal in England and Wales from 2011 to 2018, and became President of the Family Division in July 2018 upon Sir James Munby’s retirement from that office."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d00", "start": 277, "end": 312, "text": "McFarlane was born on 30 June 1954."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d00", "start": 313, "end": 443, "text": "He was educated at Shrewsbury School and studied law at Collingwood College, Durham, and graduated from Durham University in 1975."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d00", "start": 444, "end": 531, "text": "McFarlane was called to the bar (Gray's Inn) in 1977 and has been a Bencher since 2003."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d00", "start": 532, "end": 569, "text": "In 1998, he became a Queen's Counsel."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d01", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "Judges 'apprehensive ' about security , family division president Sir Andrew McFarlane tells MPs | Law Gazette Our Privacy Policy has changed ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d01", "start": 144, "end": 269, "text": "Please click here to read about how we process your data in compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation ( GDPR ) ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0294-69fc77902d97:d01", "start": 270, "end": 584, "text": "OK Skip to main content Skip to navigation The Law Society Find a